rogram requirements.\nFind out about admission requirements.\nUrban Science Doctoral Track\nTandon Ph.D. students can specialize their studies in electrical engineering with a focus on urban science through the new doctoral track offered by the Center for Urban Science + Progress.\nAbu Dhabi Global Fellow Program\nApplicants to this degree program may be eligible to participate in the Abu Dhabi Global Fellow Program\nNYU Shanghai Ph.D. Program\nDual Ph.D. Degree Program with the Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur\nQuick Links\nGraduate Admissions\nRequest Information\nStudent Resources\nQuick Links\nQuick Links\nGraduate Admissions\nRequest Information\nStudent Resources\nQuick Links\nGraduate Admissions\nRequest Information\nStudent Resources\nProgram Director\nYong Liu\nProfessor, Electrical and Computer Engineering; Director of Graduate Programs\nTandon Alumni\nRex Guo\nPh.D. Electrical Engineering, 2014\nCEO & Co-founder of Culminate\nAnthony Vetro\nElectrical Engineering Ph.D., 2001\nPresident and CEO, Mitsubishi Electric Research Laboratories (MERL)\nMain Menu\nNYU Tandon Made in Brooklyn\nQuick Links\nNYU Libraries\nNYU Brightspace\nNYU Albert\nAccessibility\nBulletin\nTandon Directory\nLogin (Faculty & Staff)\nInformation For\nStudents\nFaculty\nStaff\nAlumni\nParents\nMedia\nCareers at Tandon\nContact\nContact Us\n646-997-3600\nNYU Campuses\nNew York\nShanghai\nAbu Dhabi\nNYU Tandon Made in Brooklyn\nMake a Gift\nFollow Us\nFacebook\nThreads\nInstagram\nYoutube\nLinkedIn\nTikTok\nBlue Sky\nNew York University is committed to maintaining an environment that encourages and fosters respect for\nindividual\nvalues and appropriate conduct among all persons. In all University spaces\u2014\nphysical and digital\u2014programming, activities, and events are carried out in\naccordance with applicable law as well as University policy, which includes but\nis not limited to its Non-Discrimination\nand Anti-Harassment Policy.\n\u00a9 NYU Tandon 2026", "links": [["Skip